# Discovery Refinements

## Language Management ≠ Translation Management

Language Management is a platform capability supporting localization and multilingual user experiences across all HCGO domains.

Translation Management is a Bible Domain capability governing Bible translations (e.g., KJV, NKJV, NIV, NASB, ESV) and associated licensing, metadata, and presentation.

These capabilities shall remain architecturally independent.

---

## Reader Contact & Communication Consent

HCGO shall persist only the reader contact information and communication consent necessary to fulfill its constitutional and business responsibilities.

Communication delivery and marketing automation may be implemented through approved third-party platforms without altering the Enterprise Persistence Architecture.

---

## Enterprise Capability First

Enterprise capabilities define the architecture.

Enterprise Persistence Architecture shall be designed around enterprise business capabilities rather than backend implementation, frontend presentation, database structure, or implementation technology.

Implementation technologies shall conform to the approved architecture.

---

## Technology Independence

Enterprise Persistence Architecture is technology independent.

Implementation technologies are interchangeable and shall implement the approved Enterprise Persistence Architecture.

Technology selection shall never redefine enterprise capabilities.

---

## External Provider Integration

Specialized external providers may implement non-core enterprise services through governed integration.

Enterprise capabilities remain defined and governed by HCGO regardless of implementation provider.

Examples include:

- CRM
- Payment Processing
- Email Delivery
- Identity Providers
- Analytics Platforms

---

# Discovery Summary

This discovery establishes the stable Enterprise Capability Inventory required to support the HCGO Enterprise Persistence Architecture.

These capabilities represent long-lived enterprise responsibilities that remain independent of implementation technology and support future platform evolution without architectural redesign.

---

# Current Assessment

**Discovery Complete**

The Enterprise Capability Inventory is approved and establishes the foundation for Enterprise Capability Ownership Validation in DF-EP-003.

No physical persistence architecture, schema design, or implementation shall begin until ownership validation is completed.
